<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Feb 27.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Feb 27.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Wednesday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	   411.11   2.59</p>
<p> 2   Kidston Gold	  293.75   1.41</p>
<p> 3   Mt Edon Gold	  241.76   2.20</p>
<p> 4   Niugini Min	   241.73   3.36</p>
<p> 5   Mayne Nickless	166.84   7.56</p>
<p> 6   Adel Bton Cement    130.43   1.80</p>
<p> 7   Colonial Coml	 122.95   2.25</p>
<p> 8   St.Barbara Mine     118.31   0.84</p>
<p> 9   Westpac Prop Tr     109.37   1.75</p>
<p>10   Herald Rsc	     93.81   1.06</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	    2.14   0.93</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	   4.73   1.06</p>
<p> 3   BTR Plc		   5.86   5.45</p>
<p> 4   Parbury Ltd	     6.59   0.78</p>
<p> 5   OLS Asia Hldgs	  6.97   0.83</p>
<p> 6   Aust Gold Rsc	   7.01   1.28</p>
<p> 7   Premier Inv	     7.50   1.33</p>
<p> 8   BT Aust Eq Mgmt	 7.52   0.76</p>
<p> 9   Renison Goldflds	7.70   5.25</p>
<p>10   FAI Life ltd	    7.86   0.81</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
